{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedPresentationRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedPresentationRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraInstance","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTowerBasicConstruction","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2AlgebraInstance","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3Semisimple","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceFormSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_vacuous_of_isSemisimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_vacuous_of_isSemisimpleRing","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L406-L424","doc":"**`WenzlTowerStep` is free wherever its conclusion already holds.**\n\nGiven `IsSemisimpleRing Hn1` the field is discharged by ignoring both hypotheses,\nat any rank and any carrier. `wenzlTowerStep_H2_H3_trivial` is the `rank = 3`\nspecial case of this; `wenzlTowerStep_regTrace` is the contrasting one, where the\nnondegeneracy hypothesis genuinely does the work.\n\n🛑 **Do not cite this as the Wenzl ascent.** It proves that the class says nothing\nonce its conclusion is known, per AGENTS.md §3b-cond rule 5 — the reason no\ninstance of it was created at the `wtrace` quotient carrier, where\n`WtraceRadicalSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_traceQuot_of_hecke` makes the conclusion\nunconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_regTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_regTrace","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L339-L365","doc":"**`WenzlTowerStep` for the regular trace, at any rank.** Discharged from\nleft-nondegeneracy alone; the `IsSemisimpleRing Hn` hypothesis is discarded\nbecause it is not needed.\n\nThe semisimplicity engine is NOT proved here — it is\n`QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceForm_nondegenerate`, which the\ncorpus has carried since brick B3d (epic `qou-hnhg`). What this adds is only\nthe adapter: `WenzlTowerStep` states nondegeneracy existentially (`∀ y ≠ 0,\n∃ z, tr (y * z) ≠ 0`) where that theorem states it as a left-kernel condition\n(`∀ x, (∀ y, B x y = 0) → x = 0`). The two are contrapositives once the unary\ntrace is `w ↦ trace (L_w)`, since then `tr (y * z) = regTraceForm R Hn1 y z`.\n\nContrast `wenzlTowerStep_H2_H3_trivial`, which discards BOTH hypotheses and\ntherefore carries no content. Here the nondegeneracy hypothesis does the work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_H2_H3_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_H2_H3_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L294-L305","doc":"**`WenzlTowerStep` holds at `H₂ → H₃`, trivially.** Both hypotheses are\ndiscarded; the conclusion is `isSemisimpleRing_H3A`.\n\nStated as a theorem taking the genericity conditions explicitly rather than as an\n`instance`, for two reasons: `isSemisimpleRing_H3A` needs them, and an instance\nwould invite instance search to present a trivial discharge as though it were the\nascent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.tower_classes_inhabited_H2_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.tower_classes_inhabited_H2_H3","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L257-L272","doc":"**All four tower classes are inhabited at `H₂ ⊂ H₃`, and found by instance\nsearch.** Recorded as one statement so the milestone is checkable rather than\nasserted across four separate declarations — and so that a later change which\nquietly breaks resolution for any one of them fails here.\n\nWhat this does NOT say: nothing about general `n`. Every component is fixed at\nrank 3, and `WenzlTowerStep` is not among them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeMarkovExpectation_H2_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeMarkovExpectation_H2_H3","kind":"instance","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L250-L255","doc":"**`HeckeMarkovExpectation`, instantiated** for `H₂ ⊂ H₃` at the coset\ngenerator `σ₁`, with the Ocneanu scalar `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeConditionalExpectation_H2_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeConditionalExpectation_H2_H3","kind":"instance","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L243-L248","doc":"**`HeckeConditionalExpectation`, instantiated** for `H₂ ⊂ H₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_markov","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L229-L235","doc":"**The Markov property holds for `epsLin`** — the field of\n`HeckeMarkovExpectation`: `ε (ι b · σ₁ · ι c) = z • (b · c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_bimodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_bimodule","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L215-L227","doc":"**`bimodule` holds for `epsLin`** — the second field, concretely:\n`ε (ι x · w · ι y) = x · ε w · y` for all `x, y : H₂` and `w : H₃`.\n\nThis is the one that could have failed. `ε` was written down from the coset\ntable by imposing the Markov property; whether the resulting map is an\n`(H₂, H₂)`-bimodule map is a separate question, settled here by computation\nover all six coordinates with `x`, `y`, `w` symbolic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_retract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin_retract","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L209-L213","doc":"**`retract` holds for `epsLin`** — the first field of\n`HeckeConditionalExpectation`, concretely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsLin","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L203-L207","doc":"`epsFun` bundled as an `R`-linear map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.epsFun","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L197-L201","doc":"The conditional expectation `H₃ → H₂` at Markov parameter `z`, in\ncoordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeCosetSpanning_H2_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckeCosetSpanning_H2_H3","kind":"instance","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L159-L179","doc":"**`HeckeCosetSpanning`, instantiated.** Every `w : H₃` splits as\n`ι a + Σᵢ ι (b i) · σ₁ · ι (c i)` with the four coset terms reading off `w`'s\ncoordinates 2–5 and `a` reading off 0–1.\n\nThis is the class's first instance, and the statement is discharged by an\nexplicit decomposition rather than by any abstract argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckePresentationOfRank_H2A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckePresentationOfRank_H2A","kind":"instance","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L149-L157","doc":"Rank-2 presentation instance for `H₂(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.t0_mul_t0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.t0_mul_t0","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.gen2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.gen2","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L142-L144","doc":"Rank-2 generator family. At rank 2 the only obligation is the quadratic for\n`σ 0`; braid and far-commutation are vacuous, so indices past the rank go to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.t0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.t0","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L139-L140","doc":"`σ₀` inside the rank-2 algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_mul_s1_ne_s1_mul_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_mul_s1_ne_s1_mul_s0","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L114-L122","doc":"**The two generators do not commute.** This is what the constant family\ncannot reproduce: there, `far_commute` and `braid_adjacent` hold by `rfl`\nprecisely because everything commutes. Here the braid relation\n`σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁` is a genuine identity between two *different* products. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_ne_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_ne_s1","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L108-L112","doc":"The two generators are distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckePresentationOfRank_H3A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.heckePresentationOfRank_H3A","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L84-L99","doc":"**The corpus's first content-bearing presentation instance.** Genuine\n`H₃(q)` on the six-element normal-form basis, with its two true generators: the\nHecke quadratic for each and the braid relation between them. Nothing padded,\nnothing constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.braid_s0_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.braid_s0_s1","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L80-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s1_mul_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s1_mul_s1","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L76-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_mul_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0_mul_s0","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L72-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.gen","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L66-L70","doc":"The generator family. At rank 3 the guards constrain only `σ 0` and `σ 1`;\nindices past the rank are unconstrained, so they are sent to `0` rather than\npadded with a real generator — padding is exactly what the unbounded class\ncannot survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s1","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L63-L64","doc":"`σ₁` as an element of the normal-form algebra — basis index 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.s0","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedPresentationRank.lean#L60-L61","doc":"`σ₀` as an element of the normal-form algebra — basis index 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}